 "notes": "95% CL upper limit on the B-L gauge coupling g_{B-L} for ultra-low-mass vector dark matter, from Fig.5 (raster B-LlimitsSimple.png; no ancillary data in e-print). The plotted y-axis g_{B-L}(hc)^{-1/2} is the dimensionless gauge coupling in natural units, reported as-is (no conversion). Curve is the lower boundary of the excluded (yellow) region = lower envelope of the noisy black limit band, digitized by axis calibration (10^-24/10^-25 y-ticks, decade=217px; 10^-18/-17/-16 x-labels, decade=276.5px; frame endpoints reproduce the stated mass range 0.4e-18 to 2.07e-16 eV). Paper reports the field polarized along X, Y, Z in three near-identical panels; I averaged the three lower envelopes (log-mean) since none is singled out as the main result. Deepest g~7e-26 at m~8e-18 eV, consistent with the abstract's best g_{B-L}(hc)^{-1/2}<1e-25 at 8e-18 eV/c^2. Local DM density assumed rho_DM~0.3 GeV/cm^3 (Sec.I).",
